{
  "about": "One set of scrub cases for every Cyber Rakshak monitoring library (resources/sdk). Each library's tests run its scrub() over every 'in' and expect 'out' exactly. The rules, in order: query strings; Bearer/Basic values; password/secret/token/api-key style values (the name is kept; at most 40 more name characters after the word); JWTs (a header of at most 500 characters); known key prefixes (crk_, sk_live_, ghp_, AKIA...) not preceded by a letter or digit; email addresses (at most 64 characters before the @); IBANs (2 capitals, 2 digits, then 11-30 capitals/digits or the same in groups of four with single spaces, 15-34 in all, not touching a letter or digit, passing the ISO 13616 mod-97 check); card numbers (13-19 digits, not preceded by a digit, passing the Luhn check); whole-word names (authorization, cookie, signature, otp, pin, cvv, cvc, iban, bban, pan, account no/number/num, sort code, card number, bank auth id: not right after a letter or digit, the separator right after the name, a value of Bearer/Basic and a space left alone; the name is kept); runs of 32+ hex digits; runs of 40+ letters/digits/+_- holding a digit, an upper-case and a lower-case letter. A library's scrubNames and scrubPatterns run after these and are not in this file.",
